{"id":"a015fcd24d4b916f","group":"93","path":"93/93-cor-lowenheim-upward.md","title":"Upward Lowenheim","display":"Upward Lowenheim","type":"corollary","metadata":{"type":"corollary","book":"Algebraizable Logics","book_abbrev":"93","label":"93-cor-lowenheim-upward","aliases":["93-cor-lowenheim-upward"],"display":"Upward Lowenheim","authors":"W. J. Blok, Don Pigozzi","book_title":"Algebraizable Logics","depends_on":["[[93-df-cardinality]]","[[93-df-variety]]","[[93-df-free-algebra]]","[[93-prop-free-algebra]]","[[93-df-similarity-type]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"corollary"},{"key":"book","html":"Algebraizable Logics"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"93"},{"key":"label","html":"93-cor-lowenheim-upward"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>93-cor-lowenheim-upward</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"Upward Lowenheim"},{"key":"authors","html":"W. J. Blok, Don Pigozzi"},{"key":"book_title","html":"Algebraizable Logics"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"1734624324342672\" href=\"?note=1734624324342672\" title=\"93-df-cardinality\">93-df-cardinality</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"f0b0edbaa6696a1d\" href=\"?note=f0b0edbaa6696a1d\" title=\"93-df-variety\">93-df-variety</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"64f6348f5d9119d6\" href=\"?note=64f6348f5d9119d6\" title=\"93-df-free-algebra\">93-df-free-algebra</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"259a663bdd529644\" href=\"?note=259a663bdd529644\" title=\"93-prop-free-algebra\">93-prop-free-algebra</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"ee84ed8b0fae5bc3\" href=\"?note=ee84ed8b0fae5bc3\" title=\"93-df-similarity-type\">93-df-similarity-type</a></span></div>"}],"html":"<h1 id=\"cor-lowenheim-upward---Upward-Lowenheim\">cor-lowenheim-upward - Upward Lowenheim</h1>\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\tau=\\langle S,\\alpha\\rangle\">\\(\\tau=\\langle S,\\alpha\\rangle\\)</span> is finitary, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Variety}_{93}(\\mathcal V;\\tau)\">\\(\\mathrm{Variety}_{93}(\\mathcal V;\\tau)\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal V\">\\(\\mathcal V\\)</span> is nontrivial: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\exists\\mathbf B\\in\\mathcal V\\;\\exists b_0,b_1\\in|\\mathbf B|\\;(b_0\\ne b_1)\">\\(\\exists\\mathbf B\\in\\mathcal V\\;\\exists b_0,b_1\\in|\\mathbf B|\\;(b_0\\ne b_1)\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{InfCard}_{93}(\\kappa)\">\\(\\mathrm{InfCard}_{93}(\\kappa)\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CardLe}_{93}(S,\\kappa)\">\\(\\mathrm{CardLe}_{93}(S,\\kappa)\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SimilarityType}\">\\(\\mathrm{SimilarityType}\\)</span> is the type predicate of <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"ee84ed8b0fae5bc3\" href=\"?note=ee84ed8b0fae5bc3\" title=\"93-df-similarity-type\">93-df-similarity-type</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CardEq}\">\\(\\mathrm{CardEq}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CardLe}_{93}\">\\(\\mathrm{CardLe}_{93}\\)</span> are the equipotence and cardinal-comparison predicates of <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"1734624324342672\" href=\"?note=1734624324342672\" title=\"93-df-cardinality\">93-df-cardinality</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\tau=\\langle S,\\alpha\\rangle\\land\\mathrm{SimilarityType}(S,\\alpha)\n\\land\\mathrm{Variety}_{93}(\\mathcal V;\\tau)\n\\land\\forall f\\in S\\;\\bigl(\\alpha(f)\\in\\omega\\bigr)\n\\land\\Bigl(\\exists\\mathbf B\\in\\mathcal V\\;\\exists b_0,b_1\\in|\\mathbf B|\\;(b_0\\ne b_1)\\Bigr)\n\\land\\mathrm{InfCard}_{93}(\\kappa)\\land\\mathrm{CardLe}_{93}(S,\\kappa)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\to\\exists\\mathbf A\\in\\mathcal V\\;\\mathrm{CardEq}(|\\mathbf A|,\\kappa).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\tau=\\langle S,\\alpha\\rangle\\land\\mathrm{SimilarityType}(S,\\alpha)\n\\land\\mathrm{Variety}_{93}(\\mathcal V;\\tau)\n\\land\\forall f\\in S\\;\\bigl(\\alpha(f)\\in\\omega\\bigr)\n\\land\\Bigl(\\exists\\mathbf B\\in\\mathcal V\\;\\exists b_0,b_1\\in|\\mathbf B|\\;(b_0\\ne b_1)\\Bigr)\n\\land\\mathrm{InfCard}_{93}(\\kappa)\\land\\mathrm{CardLe}_{93}(S,\\kappa)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\to\\exists\\mathbf A\\in\\mathcal V\\;\\mathrm{CardEq}(|\\mathbf A|,\\kappa).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>Take the free algebra on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span> generators. Nontriviality separates its generators, while finitarity and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CardLe}_{93}(S,\\kappa)\">\\(\\mathrm{CardLe}_{93}(S,\\kappa)\\)</span> bound the term set above by <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span>. The formula identifies <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"S\">\\(S\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\alpha\">\\(\\alpha\\)</span> with the components of the type used by the variety.</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"cor-lowenheim-upward---Upward-Lowenheim","text":"cor-lowenheim-upward - Upward Lowenheim","level":1},{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"93-df-cardinality","status":"resolved","id":"1734624324342672","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-cardinality]]","embed":false},